# Exclude lockmodtable and modtable from HTML validity checks (ESLint and the Mustache checks
# still run, and every other template here stays fully validated).
#
# Both are page fragments, not standalone documents: their inputs carry
# form="tool_activitydates_lock_form" / form="tool_activitydates_dates_form", which
# point at the moodleform rendered earlier on the page (see
# classes/locks/form/lock_form.php and classes/form/activitydates_form.php). The linter renders the
# template on its own, where no such form exists, so the HTML validator always
# reports "The form attribute must refer to a form element" for markup that is
# correct on the real page.
lockmodtable.mustache
modtable.mustache
